    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced case for JPM. The bull case rests on a strong uptrend (price above all major moving averages, positive cumulative returns across 5d/20d/60d, minimal drawdown from peak) and a fortress balance sheet ($3.875T assets, $327.9B equity, +$55B net cash build). However, the bear case highlights a sharp +15.19% 60-day run, RSI cooling from an overbought 80.33 peak to 67.93, a negative MACD histogram (-0.10) with a bearish divergence on the March 13 high ($181.92) vs. March 15 close ($180.57), and ambiguous volume signals. Critically, there is a complete data blackout \u2014 no income statement data, no news flow, no sentiment, and no macro confirmation \u2014 which prevents validating the +15% run. With the stock extended at $180.57 and momentum rolling over, the risk/reward is roughly balanced. The prudent stance is to maintain the position without adding aggressively, waiting for either a pullback toward the 10 EMA ($178.76) or Bollinger middle ($176.39) for better entry, or fundamental confirmation from earnings/macro data. A stop below the 50 SMA ($168.80) would signal genuine trend reversal.\n\n**Entry Price**: 178.76\n\n**Stop Loss**: 168.8\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-underweight allocation relative to benchmark; do not let JPM become an outsized position until fundamental confirmation arrives.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
